# BuildKit per-Dockerfile ignore for `docker build -f web/app/Dockerfile .` (context = repo root).
# Takes precedence over the root .dockerignore (which is the .NET image's allow-list), so the
# root file does not need to change. Exclusion-based: everything out, then the web inputs back in.
*
!package.json
!pnpm-workspace.yaml
!pnpm-lock.yaml
!tests/e2e/package.json
!web/app/**
# re-exclude build output and local state inside web/app (later rules win)
**/node_modules
**/.next
web/app/.env*
!web/app/.env.example
web/app/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/next-env.d.ts
